**Design rationale summary:**

| Aspect | Decision | Reasoning |
|--------|----------|-----------|
| **Rule type** | `position_near_with_facing` | Preferred rule for find/locate/observe tasks per the milestone design philosophy. Models "player can see the target." |
| **Target** | `[7, 2, 3]` | Matches the `/setblock ~7 ~2 ~3 minecraft:green_wall_banner[facing=north]` command from the final scene revision. |
| **max_distance** | `16` | Generous range — the open terrain (cleared of trees) gives clear line of sight. The banner is ~8-9 blocks from spawn, so 16 blocks allows the player to spot it from various positions. |
| **facing_tolerance** | `60°` | Standard tolerance ensuring the player is looking roughly toward the banner (within a 120° cone), not just standing nearby while facing away. The banner faces north, so the player needs to be north of it looking south. |
| **coordinate_frame** | `"spawn_relative"` | Required per spec — all spatial rules must use spawn-relative coordinates. |
